## Vehicle Fleet at a Glance

| Vehicle | Bookings | Success Rate | Avg Distance | Total KM |
|---------|----------|-------------|--------------|----------|
| Auto | 12.88M | 91.1% | 25.99 km | 602K km |
| eBike / Bike | 11.46M | 91.1% | 26.11 km | 537K km |
| Go Mini | 10.34M | 91.0% | 25.99 km | 482K km |
| Go Sedan | 9.37M | 91.1% | 25.98 km | 433K km |
| Premier Sedan | 6.28M | 91.2% | 25.95 km | 292K km |
| **UberXL** | **1.53M** | **92.2%** | 25.72 km | 72K km |

> UberXL's 92.2% success rate is the highest in the fleet despite the lowest booking volume — its riders are more intentional and less likely to cancel.

---

## Cancellation Deep Dive

**Why customers cancel:**

| Reason | Share |
|--------|-------|
| Wrong Address | 22.5% |
| Driver Issues | 22.4% |
| Driver Not Moving | 22.2% |
| Change of Plans | 21.9% |
| App Issues | 11.0% |

**Why drivers cancel:**

| Reason | Share |
|--------|-------|
| Customer-Related Issues | 25.3% |
| Capacity Issues | 25.0% |
| Personal & Car Issues | 24.9% |
| Customer Behavior | 24.8% |

Both sides show near-uniform distributions — no single cause dominates on either end. This is systemic friction, not isolated incidents.

---

## Rating Summary

| Vehicle Type | Customer Rating | Driver Rating |
|---|---|---|
| Go Sedan | **4.41** | 4.24 |
| Auto | 4.40 | 4.23 |
| Go Mini | 4.40 | 4.23 |
| eBike / Bike | 4.40 | 4.23 |
| Premier Sedan | 4.40 | 4.24 |
| UberXL | 4.40 | **4.24** |

The 0.01 spread across all six vehicle types is not differentiation — it is compression. The rating system is not surfacing meaningful quality signals.

---

## Key Takeaways

```
┌──────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Supply           │ ~11K "No Driver Found" is a platform-wide shortage,         │
│                  │ not a zone or category issue                                │
├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Cancellations    │ ~27K driver cancels split evenly across four causes —       │
│                  │ requires four parallel fixes, not one                       │
├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Revenue          │ Auto + Go Mini = ~₹2.33Cr combined; eBike + UberXL = ~₹51L│
├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Pricing          │ Distance (r=0.42) is the only meaningful fare predictor;   │
│                  │ vehicle type and surge matter more                          │
├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Demand           │ 18:00 is the peak hour; weekends generate ~50% more        │
│                  │ revenue than any weekday                                    │
├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Payments         │ UPI leads real transactions; ~48K records unclassified      │
├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Ratings          │ Both sides inflate — a 4.0 is a warning, not a midpoint    │
└──────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Recommendations

**① Fix the cancellation system — not just the symptoms**
- Capture group size at booking to eliminate overcrowding cancellations before they happen
- Introduce dynamic cancellation penalties to disincentivise selective ride rejection
- Build a driver wellness scheduling system to reduce personal/car-related abandonment

**② Close the supply gap with precision**
- Map every "No Driver Found" event to its time and zone — deploy targeted incentives exactly there
- Pre-position drivers in the 17:00–19:00 window using demand forecasting; do not rely on passive surge

**③ Capture the weekend premium properly**
- Activate weekend-specific driver bonus schemes to ensure supply scales with the ~50% demand spike
- Launch a Friday evening campaign — this is the most undercaptured demand window in the dataset

**④ Fix the data before drawing more conclusions**
- Reclassify ~48K "Not Applicable" payment records — payment analysis is unreliable until this is resolved
- Add sub-reasons to "Customer-Related" driver cancellations — the current label is too broad to act on
- Enrich future datasets with: surge multiplier · zone-level supply ratio · driver tenure · vehicle age

**⑤ Invest in what works, deprioritise what doesn't**
- Auto and Go Mini are the revenue engine — protect supply, reduce cancellations, strengthen incentives
- Uber Wallet is an underutilised loyalty lever — wallet users are your highest-value repeat customers
- eBike and Uber XL need a formal strategic review — they are not self-sustaining at current volumes

---

## Use Cases

This dataset is well-suited for:

- `Cancellation Prediction` — classify pre-trip cancellation risk before a driver accepts
- `Revenue Forecasting` — time-series modelling of daily and weekly booking value
- `Supply-Demand Modelling` — map "No Driver Found" events to zone and hour for targeted intervention
- `Driver Segmentation` — cluster by rating, cancel rate, earnings, and vehicle type
- `Customer Segmentation` — segment by vehicle preference, payment method, and booking frequency
- `Surge Pricing Analysis` — model fare variance unexplained by distance to surface surge patterns
- `Rating System Research` — study bilateral rating behaviour and inflation at scale

